The onNavigate promise logic I wrote is convoluted garbage (`(ok) => setConfirmNav(null) || ok && void 0` — awful). Let me write it cleanly: navRef stores a function that sets confirmNav with a resolver that clears itself:

```ts
navRef.current = (path) => {
  setConfirmNav({
    path,
    resolve: (ok) => { setConfirmNav(null); },
  });
};
```
But the Promise needs to resolve(ok) — the ChatPanel calls onNavigateAnswer(ok) → confirmNav.resolve(ok). So the resolve stored in confirmNav must BOTH resolve the promise AND clear the bar. Restructure:

```ts
navRef.current = (path) => new Promise<boolean>((resolve) => {
  setConfirmNav({ path, resolve: (ok) => { resolve(ok); setConfirmNav(null); } });
});
```
And onNavigateAnswer={(ok) => confirmNav?.resolve(ok)} already exists. Then remove the onNavigate wiring inside createExecutor options to: `onNavigate: (path) => navRef.current(path)` where navRef.current: (path) => Promise<boolean>.

